  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "Pictures sent to the famous astronomer Carl Sagan at Cornell University in the 1980s never reached him, according to John Brandenburg, a physicist who argues that Mars once had life. Brandenburg says he later asked Sagan what he thought of the pictures, and Sagan answered, \"I never got them.\" He tells it as a hint that the material was stopped before it could reach Sagan."
